 "text": [
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "text": "laver (Porphyra umbilicalis)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "The closest species with at least 100 curator-checked (Swiss-Prot) proteins is Porphyra purpurea; TimeTree has no age for when the two lineages split. No tool on this board was measured at this distance. In the measured organism closest to this one, human (Homo sapiens), 15% of proteins had no hit from any sequence tool, so expect a share like that to stay without a label."
  },
  {
   "tag": "pre",
   "text": "# laver (Porphyra umbilicalis) # UniProt reference proteome UP000218209, 13,469 proteins curl -L -o proteome.fasta.gz 'https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/stream?query=proteome%3AUP000218209&format=fasta&compressed=true' # All reviewed Swiss-Prot proteins, the source of the labels (they include those of the nearest reviewed relative, Porphyra purpurea). # Swiss-Prot has about 575,000 proteins; the board measured cost against one relative's proteome of about 20,000, so expect longer runs. curl -L -o swissprot.fasta.gz 'https://ftp.uniprot.org/pub/databases/uniprot/current_release/knowledgebase/complete/uniprot_sprot.fasta.gz' # nf-core/proteinannotator 1.1.0: Pfam, FunFam and InterProScan on your proteome. # Version 1.1.0 has no option to run the tools below; their commands follow. printf 'id,fasta\\nporphyra_umbilicalis,proteome.fasta.gz\\n' > samplesheet.csv nextflow run nf-core/proteinannotator -r 1.1.0 -profile docker --input samplesheet.csv --outdir results"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Four facts about this species"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Three tools, in the order to run them"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "No verdict: TimeTree gives no age between this species and its nearest reviewed relative, so the page cannot place it at a distance."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "What no tool on this board will find for you"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "15.1% of 20,600 proteins of human (Homo sapiens) had no hit from any sequence tool, even at a loose E-value below 1 (the E-value is the number of hits that size expected by chance). They were searched against Swiss-Prot with the organism's own group removed; we call these proteins dark. Of the five organisms measured, this one is closest to this species: their lineages meet at Eukaryota."
  },
  {
   "tag": "th",
   "text": "Part of the dark share"
  },
  {
   "tag": "th",
   "text": "Measured"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "no relative in Swiss-Prot (no hit at all)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "15.1%"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "disordered (no stable fold)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "— not run"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "short motif only"
  },
  {
   "tag": "td",
   "text": "— not run"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "The tables hold the dark share but do not split it into disordered proteins and short motifs; those two parts are not measured. Measured on: human (Homo sapiens) 15.1% of 20,600; baker's yeast (Saccharomyces cerevisiae) 21.5% of 6,049; nematode (Caenorhabditis elegans) 45.0% of 19,819; Lyme disease bacterium (Borrelia burgdorferi) 47.4% of 1,291; star ascidian (Botryllus schlosseri) 45.1% of 45,339."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Expected to get a label"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "— Cannot be estimated: no verdict."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Figures"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Where every number comes from"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Tool scores and costs: results.parquet and compute.parquet, seanome/2024-kmerseek-analysis commit 7eca428b, experiment qfo_region_midi_plus. cost_usd_est is an estimate: CPU-hours times the AWS on-demand price (c7i.large $0.08925 per hour for 2 vCPU and g5.xlarge $1.006 per GPU-hour, US East, read 2026-10-15), plus GPU-hours times the GPU price. Lookups for the four facts:"
  },
  {
   "tag": "th",
   "text": "lookup"
  },
  {
   "tag": "th",
   "text": "release"
  },
  {
   "tag": "th",
